  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "The Skill Panel board has limited Skill Points per character—prioritise the outer ring skills that provide passive stat boosts (HP+50, MP+30) before filling inner-ring active abilities, as stat passives compound across the entire game length.",
      "Pep Powers (Oomph abilities) activate when two or more party members are simultaneously Pepped Up—maintain a mental note of which Pep combinations your team can perform and stack these against boss HP thresholds.",
      "Act 2 introduces Super Strong Monsters with significantly higher HP and drops than standard variants—these are marked with a red aura and respawn with each campfire rest. Farming Super Strong Monsters in Heliodor Region provides the best gold income for equipment in early Act 2.",
      "The Draconian Quest modifiers (Enemies Are Stronger, No Experience Points) permanently alter difficulty—select these at game start only if targeting a challenge run; they cannot be removed mid-playthrough without a new game.",
      "Crafting via the Fun-Size Forge provides the best early equipment at no purchase cost—prioritise forging recipes from treasure chests over buying from shops, as forged items at maximum crafting quality exceed shop equivalents by 15–20 attack/defense."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "スキルパネルはキャラクターごとにスキルポイントが限られている。外周リングのパッシブステータスアップ（HP+50、MP+30）をアクティブアビリティより優先する。ゲーム全体でパッシブステータスが積み重なる。",
      "ペップパワーは2人以上が同時にペップアップ状態の時に発動する。チームが使えるペップの組み合わせを把握し、ボスのHP閾値に合わせてスタックする。",
      "第2部ではスーパーモンスターが登場し、通常個体より大幅に高いHPとドロップを持つ。赤いオーラで識別でき、たき火での休憩ごとに再スポーン。ヘリオドール周辺のスーパーモンスターファーミングが第2部序盤の最良のゴールド収入源。",
      "ドラゴシークエストの縛り（ボス強化、経験値なし）は難易度を永続的に変更する。これらはチャレンジランを目指す場合のみゲーム開始時に選択する。途中での削除はニューゲームが必要。",
      "ふしぎなかじやは最善の序盤装備を無料で提供する。宝箱からのレシピのクラフトをショップ購入より優先する。最高クラフト品質の鍛造品はショップ品と比べて攻撃/防御が15〜20高い。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Early Skill Panel Priority",
        "body": "For Luminary (the protagonist), prioritise the Greatsword panel branch first: it leads to Gigaslash and then the Pep Power activator skills that are crucial for mid-game. Sylvando's panel should focus on the Hustle Dance branch (heals all party members for a medium amount each)—Hustle Dance replaces the need for dedicated healers in most fights. Erik's panel should target Divide (doubles the next physical attack's damage) above all other skills in early game."
      },
      {
        "title": "Campsite and Item Management",
        "body": "Camp at every available campsite rather than using inns whenever possible—camping is free and provides the same recovery. The cooking mechanic at campsites produces stat-buffing food with limited charges per recipe; cooking Kamikaze Braised Beef (mid-game recipe) before boss fights provides 5 turns of attack boost for the whole party. Always maintain a stock of 10+ Medicinal Herbs and 5+ Antidotes before entering dungeons, as the early game has limited access to MP-efficient healing."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Party Composition Adjustment",
        "body": "Post-Act 2 party composition should always include: Sylvando (Hustle Dance healer), Erik (Divide + DPS), and two characters based on boss element. Jade becomes the highest physical DPS in the game after unlocking Multithrust (Spear panel) and Eclipse (Whip panel); build her in parallel with the main team. Rab's Hocus-Pocus (Random Pep effect) provides a 1-in-8 chance of activating Yggdragon's Blessing (full party resurrection)—useful in extremely long boss fights where attrition becomes the primary challenge."
      },
      {
        "title": "Casino and Medal Rewards",
        "body": "The Puerto Valor Casino becomes available in Act 2. The most efficient token farming method is Slime Quest (slot machine game)—at expert level it produces 200–500 tokens per 10 minutes. Casino tokens exchange for Bunny Suit armour (best in slot for Act 2 female characters) and Fizzle Foil (nullifies all enemy spell effects for one turn). The Baccarat and L'Academia casinos have higher jackpots but lower token-per-minute yields than Slime Quest."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Act 3 Postgame Objectives",
        "body": "Act 3 (available after completing the main story on the true ending path) is the primary endgame content block. It contains all post-game bosses and the true ending cutscene. Priority: complete all character side stories first (each unlocks a unique skill board panel), then tackle Calasmos (the true final boss). Calasmos has three forms—prepare 20+ Yggdrasil Dew (instant party full revival) and a party averaging level 90+ before attempting. The postgame crafting target is four pieces of Supreme Sword of Light equipment for maximum stat ceiling."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Buying equipment from shops when forged equivalents are available—the Fun-Size Forge produces items at lower gold cost and higher base stats than shop equivalents at every game stage.",
      "Not redistributing Skill Panel points mid-game—the game provides one free Skill Point reset per character via the Rectification of Errors service in Cobblestone; use this to correct early panel investment mistakes.",
      "Ignoring Pep Up passive skills on the panel—the chance of entering Pep Up state per turn doubles with the Pep Up passive skill; characters with this skill reach Pep Up state in approximately 3 fewer turns on average.",
      "Attempting Malicious (Act 2 enemy variants) without level parity—Malicious monsters are 15–20 levels above their Act 1 counterparts; fighting them at equivalent Act 1 level results in frequent one-shots.",
      "Skipping the Wheel of Harma trial challenges—these optional time-trial gauntlets provide the best accoutrements (neck armour) in the game; completing all 5 tiers provides near-endgame accessory quality in mid-Act 2."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ふしぎなかじやの鍛造品が入手可能な時にショップで装備を購入する。ふしぎなかじやはゲームの全段階でショップ品より低コストかつ高基礎ステータスのアイテムを生産する。",
      "中盤にスキルパネルポイントを再分配しない。ゲームはコスタコルドのエラー修正サービスでキャラクターごとに1回無料のスキルポイントリセットを提供する。序盤のパネル投資ミスを修正するために使う。",
      "パネル上のペップアップのパッシブスキルを無視する。ペップアップのパッシブスキルで毎ターンのペップアップ状態になる確率が2倍になる。このスキルを持つキャラクターは平均して約3ターン早くペップアップ状態になる。",
      "凶悪（第2部敵変種）をレベル格差なしで挑む。凶悪モンスターは第1部の対応モンスターより15〜20レベル高い。同等の第1部レベルでは頻繁にワンショットされる。",
      "ハルマの試練チャレンジをスキップする。これらのオプションのタイムトライアルはゲーム最良のアクセサリ（首装備）を提供する。全5段階の完了で第2部中盤に終盤クラスのアクセサリ品質が手に入る。"
